title: Average
golf: 38

Write `average(nums)` that returns the average of a list of numbers.
An empty list should give `0` (not a crash!).
=== starter
def average(nums):
    ...
=== broken
def average(nums):
    return sum(nums) / len(nums)
=== test
from harness import eq


def test_average(sol):
    eq(sol.average([2, 4, 6]), 4, "average([2, 4, 6])")
    eq(sol.average([1, 2]), 1.5, "average([1, 2])")
    eq(sol.average([]), 0, "average([])")
